I'm having a problem with my DCE client (HP-uX 9.04/DCE 1.2.1) "losing"
track of CDS (running on a HP-UX 10.10/DCE 1.4.1) across a WAN.

Symtoms are something like this:

  1. Stop then start client and server daemons and everything is fine.
  2. After a period of time (around 8 hours but I'm not sure) the
     client (using 'dceping') can no longer locate CDS.

A couple of related facts:

  1. During the dce_config to initially install, the script did prompt
     for the location of CDS because it correctly determined CDS was
     not on the LAN.  dce_config informed me it would use the info for
     a 'cdscp define cached server' command.
  2. Even during those times when 'dceping' fails (i.e. my client has
     lost track of CDS server), a 'cdscp show cached server machinename'
     seems to work properly on the client.
  3. On my client on a reboot I do the following in /etc/rc:
        - first, /etc/rc.dce
        - second cdscp define cached server machinename

I'm getting confused.  On the server side, when CDS comes up it get
a port assigned.  Will it keep it indefinitely in the port mapper data
base ?  Is there some piece of information that becomes stale in the
client ?  Any help would be much appreciated !

-- 
Jeff
