> I'm getting confused.  On the server side, when CDS comes up it get
> a port assigned.  Will it keep it indefinitely in the port mapper data
> base ?  Is there some piece of information that becomes stale in the
> client ?  Any help would be much appreciated !
> 

No, the cdsd-specific endpoints are registered each time cdsd
starts up.  If you disable the server gracefully, the endpoints
are removed.  You may have stale endpoints if the server dies
unexpectedly.

As long as a "cdscp dump clerk cache" shows CACHED CLEARINGHOUSES
information, you should be fine operationally on the client side.
Any delays are either stale clearinghouse info in the cache
(check the address towers), network-related delays, or the remote
CDS server is down or inaccessible via the endpoint mapper.

--Roger
 
