In article <5a15to$i7q@hyperion.nitco.com>, underdog@netnitco.net (Michael Curran) writes:
> Okay,
> 
>   Lets see if anyone knows this answer. I am using qpop2.2 and am having 
> problems with 'temp file, do you own it?' errors. When I check the statistic 
> logging for popper it tells me that there are 'too many users logged on'. 
> 

 Most DEC systems ship with a 2-user license (OSF-USR license pak).  You
 may want to check your license pak to make sure this isn't the limiting
 factor here.

   $ su
   # lmf list

 The 'maxusers' parameter in the kernel config is primarily used to size
 the kernel data structures (e.g. file descriptor tables, process table, and
 so on).  This parameter doesn't impose per say a direct limit on the 
 number of users on the system.

 In the case of the qpop2.2 software, the 'temp file' error message may
 indicate that their is some type of file locking problem.  I would check
 to qpop source to be sure.

