In article <01bbe733$e5534a90$0a0000c0@decprixl> "Darren Krome" <sterling@ozemail.com.au> writes:

>   How do I make the files they create be
>   rwx for the group automatically.

Have your users set umask to something like 002 or 007.  This will
typically result in group bits of rw-.  You probably don't want
anything they would create with vi to be executable :-).  man umask
for more info.

