As another poster mentioned, you can indeed use 'scu' to 'verify media'
of your swap partition.

However, the virtual address you give for the crash is in user space.
Can you bring the machine up very slowly (single user mode, bcheckrc,
update, then execute each file in the /sbin/rc2.d and /sbin/rc3.d
individually)? You would be able to determine exactly what was causing
the crash, and you might be able to get a crash dump which you could
analyse on another machine. (I suppose DEC won't be interested in a v2.0
problem!).

