mime-version: 1.0
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.misc
x-mailer: Mozilla 3.01 (Win95; I)


I am looking for any information regarding a painless process in having
a DCE user modify their password before or after password expiration.  
The scenario is:

1) Company policy is that a user must change their password every 90   
days
2) DCE allows you to set a password expiration/lifetime policy
3) If a user does not voluntarily change password within this time frame 
   (with no prior notice from DCE) the account/principal is forever
   disabled

One alternative is to use the password override, but that then disables
the requirement to change a password.  It appears that for each user
that doesn't change their password in a "timely" manner an administrator
will have to manually re-create or re-activate a user's account.

Any insights into this issue?  Is there something simple I am not
seeing?

Thanks,
John Adams
johadams@dttus.com



